nce":["file_impact is empty"],"finding":"No file_impact declared on a leaf work ticket.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f2b56a0701da43def","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"n6324407e6516f811","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Record the {path, reason} files this work will touch (e.g. via set_file_impact) so the attestation is scoped to them.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reword AC2 to make explicit that the author resolves each admitted key's sunset ticket status manually against the tracker (the --check command only enumerates admitted keys; it does not and must not report ticket status).","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T9"],"criteria":["E6"],"decision":"indeterminate","decision_margin":-0.95,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["AC2: 'reports zero admitted keys whose sunset ticket is closed'","'What is NOT the remedy': 'the lint-time ratchet runs in checkouts where the tickets ref need not be fetched, so resolving an id there would add a dependency it does not have'","AC2 self-corrects with 'This is a one-off verification by the author', but the verb 'reports' still attributes ticket-status knowledge to the command"],"finding":"AC2 says `check_mechanism_delta.py --check` 'reports zero admitted keys whose sunset ticket is closed', but the plan's own 'What is NOT the remedy' section establishes the ratchet does NOT read the tickets store — so the command cannot report sunset-ticket status. The sunset-ticket-closed check is a manual author cross-reference, not command output; the AC phrasing conflates the two.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fda408e77dce96bef","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria, line 2","norm_id":"n58933d4ee834004e","priority":0.0,"reason":"no-verification","recalled":false,"scenarios":["An executor r